Package: panasonic-hbtn-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-generic
Description: Panasonic Toughbook/Toughpad tablet button driver (DKMS source)
 Kernel driver for the tablet buttons of the Panasonic Toughbook CF-18 and
 CF-19 (ACPI device MAT001F/MAT0020, "TBTN") and the Toughpad FZ-G1 (MAT002A/
 MAT002B).  The firmware queues one code per
 button press or release; the driver turns them into key events and reports the
 swivel screen position as the SW_TABLET_MODE switch.  It also exposes the
 current position as the read-only sysfs file
 /sys/bus/acpi/devices/MAT0020:00/tablet_mode.
 .
 The module is built for the running kernel by DKMS.

Package: panasonic-cf19-support
Architecture: all
Depends: panasonic-hbtn-dkms (= ${binary:Version}),
         convertible-helper (>= 1.2.0),
         patch,
         python3,
         udev,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 48~), pipewire-bin
Description: Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 hardware support for GNOME on Debian
 Settings and helpers that make a Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 work on a stock
 Debian GNOME desktop:
 .
  * a relay service for the Fujitsu USB touch panel: it applies the
    calibration and presents the panel as a real touchscreen, so GNOME
    rotates the touch mapping with the display (udev rule and systemd
    service, applied only when the DMI product name is a CF-19);
  * a GNOME Shell extension that handles the tablet buttons: the keyboard
    button shows and hides the on-screen keyboard (the keyboard pops up on its
    own only in tablet position, set by convertible-helper, which also handles
    the rotation and "security" buttons);
  * a patch to PipeWire's speaker mixer path so the internal speaker is
    audible (on this machine the speaker is driven through the codec's
    Headphone element);
  * a GSettings default that enables the extension for every user.
 .
 The speaker patch is applied only on a CF-19, through a dpkg diversion that
 is removed again when the package is removed.
